"darkfred" <davisongeorge@gmail.com> wrote:
>That is with the normal rand() routine there are a maximum of (2^16-1)
>/ 2 versions of the dungeon at each level. This is not a large number,
>and in practice it is actually much smaller because one property of
>numbers produced with LGC is that they repeat when even moduluses are
>applied and have a high level of pattern in the low bits. (one element
>of which the /2 accounts for already)

Nethack is designed to avoid using rand() if it possibly can, preferring
instead to use either Berkeley random() or System V lrand48().

The period of Berkeley random() is 16*((2^31)-1).

